{
  "title": "Auto-pass loop retries 20x against dead bridge after game ends",
  "description": "When the game ends and the bridge processor shuts down, \
the auto-pass loop in `auto_pass.py` catches `ToolExecutionError` but \
retries 20 times with 5s sleeps (~100s total) before hitting the \
`MAX_CONSECUTIVE_ERRORS` limit and exiting.\n\
\n\
The error message is always \"Bridge processor is shut down\" — this is an \
unrecoverable error that should trigger an immediate exit rather than 20 \
retries.\n\
\n\
Evidence:\n\
- ~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260326_075453/MiniMx Tinker_pilot.log: lines \
353-394, 20 failed pass_priority calls from 08:42:19 to 08:43:54\n\
- ~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260326_075453/MiniMx Tinker_mcp.log: lines \
265-286, 20x \"Bridge processor is shut down\" errors\n\
\n\
Source: `src/magebench/pilot/auto_pass.py:62-68` — the `except \
ToolExecutionError` branch increments a counter and sleeps instead of checking \
if the error indicates a permanently dead bridge.\n\
\n\
Suggested fix: Check for \"shut down\" or similar unrecoverable-error markers \
in the exception message and exit immediately rather than retrying.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "pilot",
